[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115850,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoma is a benign myofibroblastic proliferation within an extensively myxoid ground substance without other epithelial or mesenchymal (nerve sheath) elements and not affecting gnathic bone.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115851,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8840/0 Myxoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115852,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "<p >XH6Q84 Myxoma, NOS</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-17T14:59:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115853,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> peripheral odontogenic myxoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115854,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115855,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxomas affect the periauricular soft tissues (external auditory canal), sinonasal tract, and larynx {8116795; 22306211; 8334970; 21938690; 25606843; 26915162; 29988276; 31032655}. They appear to arise in the soft tissue but may expand to involve adjacent bone. When multiple myxomas are present (skin of the external ear canal, eyelids), Carney complex may be present {7640202; 8116795; 16267413}. See also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/52/160\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Odontogenic myxoma</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115856,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxoma manifests as a slow-growing, site-specific swelling {8116795; 22306211}. Symptoms may be related to local tumour extension into adjacent structures (middle ear, palate, orbit, and/or nasal cavity) {8116795; 8334970; 16267413; 19221255; 22306211; 26915162; 32066550; 32525735; 33829881}. Endoscopic and radiographic images demonstrate a mass, often well delimited. Sinonasal tract tumours may show an intraosseous unilocular/multilocular radiolucency {6302014; 21168253; 21938690; 24429059; 15364495; 15701983; 27398121; 30484069; 31032655}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115857,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myxomas are rare, reported most commonly in children, although all ages may be affected, with an equal sex distribution {8116795; 8334970; 6302014; 15364495; 21168253; 21880053; 22306211; 24429059; 21624835; 15701983; 26915162; 30484069; 32525735; 33829881}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115858,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Carney complex, if present, is commonly associated with germline inactivating mutations in <em>PRKAR1A</em> and shows myxomas, spotty pigmentation, endocrine overactivity, and schwannoma {7640202; 8116795; 16267413}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115859,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p >The pathogenetic relationship between odontogenic myxoma and sinonasal myxoma is unclear {15364495; 21624835; 21168253; 30484069}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-17T15:00:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115860,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours show a grey-white, glistening surface with a gelatinous to firm consistency. They can be as large as 50&nbsp;mm but are usually &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm {8116795}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115861,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Myxomas are circumscribed but unencapsulated and are composed of a loose hypocellular proliferation of spindled, stellate, or round cells within a myxoid stroma containing arciform thin blood vessels and scattered fine collagen bands. Pleomorphism, mitotic figures, and tumour necrosis are absent {8116795; 8334970; 6302014}. Epithelial basaloid buds from the surface epithelium may be seen in lesions of the external auditory canal in patients with Carney complex. Odontogenic epithelium is absent in sinonasal tract tumours {24429059; 30484069}. Immunohistochemistry is non-contributory, with variable SMA and nuclear &beta;-catenin reactivity {30484069; 21624835}.</p>\r\n<p>In the differential diagnosis, angiomyxoma is a unique entity (CD34-reactive), and odontogenic myxomas are separated on the basis of anatomical tumour centring. Aural polyp and myxoid laryngeal polyp may have some histological overlap, but they also have inflammatory components.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-17T15:00:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115862,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115863,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115864,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a circumscribed myxoid mass with scattered stellate and spindled cells in a capillary-rich myxoid matrix; not arising in gnathic bones.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> nuclear &beta;-catenin staining (in selected cases).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115865,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T11:20:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115866,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 356,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "<p>These lesions are benign, but recurrences are common {7640202; 8116795; 30484069; 21624835; 24429059; 6302014}. External auditory canal tumours should prompt screening for Carney complex {7640202; 16267413; 22306211}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-17T15:00:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]